      "message": "feat(post): Sodick LN2W posts a constant taper as 4-axis G74 (TP / TN, U V)\n\nThe LN2W post writes a constant taper in the AQ600L owner's 4-axis form\n(#4075): after the C word, TP (the part's bottom above the worktable),\nTN (the part's top above the worktable) and G74; each cut as G01 X Y U V\nwith X Y on the part's bottom and U V the top minus the bottom; G75\nbefore T90. The start order of #4065 does not change.\n\n- The app sends WireGuideLower / WireGuideUpper / WireBottom / WireTop\n  (work Z) before a guide-offset leaning section. The post moves U V\n  from the guide planes to the part's planes along the same wire.\n- TP comes from a new declared post option, partBottomAboveTable\n  (default -1, not stated: each taper is refused by name). One height\n  for the program: a taper from a second setup is refused.\n- Refused by name in a taper: the G51 / G52 angle form, an arc, the\n  control's wire offset, a cut that ends leaning, a stream without the\n  planes.\n- New golden edm_test_taper.nc; the non-taper goldens do not change.\n\nFixes #4075\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
